profile: runtime-mirust.retired-long-term-memory.v1
updated_utc: 2026-09-23T15:16:37Z

current_truth:
  Runtime.MiRust.com is retired as a separate documentation authority.
  TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the current developer documentation portal.
  TinyRustLM.com is the current browser-local Rust/WASM app.

owner_delivery_policy_2026_09_23:
  authority: The owner explicitly requires source check-ins, local validation, and existing FTP/FTPS website publication without charged GitHub features.
  github: Use GitHub for source control only. Do not enable or run GitHub Actions, hosted CI, runners, or other charged GitHub features. Do not change billing or account settings.
  validation: Build and test locally. Record failures, unavailable tools, and skipped checks explicitly; a source commit is not a passing release result.
  checkins: Check in coherent pending source and push it as a source checkpoint even when a separately recorded release gate remains open. This supersedes older wording that blocked source check-ins until physical retirement or publication completion.
  publication: Publish websites through the existing authorized FTP/FTPS hosting workflow after verifying the exact site target and payload. Do not substitute a GitHub publishing service.
  runtime_boundary: The recorded Runtime FileZilla target is misbound to the developer portal and remains unusable. Existing atomic-activation prose is an unverified proposal to reconcile with actual FTP/FTPS capabilities, not proof that those capabilities exist.
  limits: No publication is performed by this checkpoint. Source-control authorization does not permit retrying policy-blocked deletion, using the wrong hosting target, hiding failed checks, or claiming unmeasured model or public-site success.

historical_memory:
  repository: https://github.com/MichaelKappel/Runtime.MiRust.com
  corpus_history_commit: d395307
  note: Retired documentation and its duplicated implementation snapshots belong in Git history. Keep current guidance here and compact immutable verification receipts in verification/receipts.
  cleanup_state: See .uai/short-term-memory.uai for verified physical removal versus pending policy-blocked cleanup.

redirect_behavior:
  root: https://tinyrustlm.mirust.com/developer-portal/
  docs_prefix: https://tinyrustlm.mirust.com/docs/
  llms_txt: https://tinyrustlm.mirust.com/llms.txt
  llms_full_txt: https://tinyrustlm.mirust.com/llms-full.txt

boundaries:
  - Project servers do not run user model bytes.
  - The owner authorizes MiniModel.org to serve the initial verified current SLM2 seeds; developer model payloads belong only in D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM.
  - TinyRustLM should restore a usable cached model or automatically acquire a small qualified MiniModel starter. Local files, Hugging Face, conversion and manual peer/IP controls belong in Advanced.
  - Seed authorization and source changes do not prove real model quality, live seeding or deployment.
  - Historical Runtime.MiRust.com claims are Git history, not current product authority.
